Patrick,

If you can upgrade your OSF/1 workstations, the v3.0 DECladebug debugger, 
available as part of the Developer's Toolkit on the OSF/1 CD, supports
Fortran 77 and Fortran 90. Let me supply a little more detail.  For Fortran, 
DECladebug:

	- provides access to COMMON blocks
	- supports Fortran 90 derived-type variables
	- understands Fortran RECORD variables
	- understands most Fortran data types
	- does much, much more - but you'll have to see the user's manual
	  for details.

More Fortran support is in the pipeline for future releases.  (support
for alternate entry points, for one example.)

   DECladebug (in 3.0) also:

	- accepts the dbx command set
	- supports C, C++, FORTRAN-77, FORTRAN-90, Ada, and COBOL
	- supports debugging threads
	- attaches/detaches to/from running processes
	- comes with EMACS integration support
	- has significant performance improvements over 2.0
	- contains even more

   In particular, we've made significant improvements in our startup
times and our memory consumption.  We now do much better with large 
programs than we did on 2.0.  (We've seen some monsters, too - and some
of those monsters are now part of our regular testbed.)

   If you get FUSE, you can also get an integrated Motif GUI for 
DECladebug.  
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Jeff Diewald			EASYNET:   VIRRUS::DIEWALD
	DECladebug group		INTERNET:  diewald@virrus.zko.dec.com
	Digital Equipment Corp.

Note: I don't read every article in this group.  If you have debugger 
questions, I may be able to get you an answer.  You're much more likely to 
get an answer if you put "Debug" somewhere in your subject line.


