    sc> The maximum length of most Unix command line buffers is, what 1K?

This used to be true of some UNIX systems, but all modern versions of
UNIX have a very large possible "command line" (and environment).  Max
sizes are almost always at least 20K now.  On HP/UX it's 20K, on AIX
it's 24K, and on SunOS (4.1.3) and Solaris it's a whole megabyte!

