>"DIR *.*" will generate a listing of all files in the current directory.

as will "DIR *"

>"COPY *.* B:" will copy all files in the current directory to the default
>directory of the B: drive.  In both cases, files which have the "hidden"
>bit set will be excluded.

On the other hand, "COPY * B:" will only copy files without extension.
Similarly, "DEL *" will delete all files without extension without asking,
while "DEL *.*" will delete all files after asking ("all files will be
deleted"), while "DEL a*.*: won't ask, even when all files _do_ start with
an 'A'.

"PRINT" behaves like copy and del as well. "ATTRIB" is an exception in that
its wildcards include hidden/system files. "CHKDSK" doesn't see hidden
files, even when the name is given explicitly --- "TYPE" does.

But don't expect a pattern here (like "DIR" is broken, everything else
