SHARE is holding its winter technical conference in Los Angeles the
week of February 26th to March 3, 1995.  Open systems and DCE represent
some of the major topical programs available at each SHARE Conference. 
At the Winter 85 SHARE Conference you will find a wide variety of 
technical presentations for both the DCE novice and the DCE system 
professional.  Below is a brief description of the DCE track, there
are similar tracks on AIX, multiprotocol networking, The Internet, 
super computing, and general UNIX topics.  If you are seeking ways to 
increase your DCE technical skills and knowledge , or want to build a 
network of DCE technical associates than please consider attending 
this winters SHARE Conference.

The Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) is a group of
client-server application enabling technologies from the Open Software
Foundation.  These technologies are available from virtually all open
system vendors and support all of the major computer architectures and
operating systems.  Using DCE middleware it's possible to write truly
seamless applications that transparently use the resources of all
computer platforms in your network.  SHARE's DCE track will introduce
you to the core technologies and distributed file services in DCE.
There will be sessions on DCE administration, security, designing
distributed applications, application development tools, and a hands
on lab to use in really understanding what is required to write DCE
applications.  You will also have the opportunity to discover DCE
capability on all IBM computer platforms, and to explore the role for
MVS in a DCE environment.  Finally there are sessions to introduce the
capabilities and complexities of the CICS/6000 API and the ENCINA
transaction monitor and structured file system.  So come learn about
these DCE based tools for creating heterogeneous on-line transaction
processing applications.  Examples of a few session names from this
26 session track:

   2910 Overview of DCE Technology - Core Services
   2920 DCE User Experience
   2922 DCE Administration
   2930 DCE Application Development Tools
   2941 DCE Hands-on Programming Lab - Part 1 of 2

For the full DCE agenda, complete conference information, and conference 
registration forms you are invited to point your gopher browser to 
gopher@share.org, or for WWW access use URL http://www.share.org/.  You 
may contact SHARE via email by writing to sharehq@share.org or phone 
SHARE at (312) 822-0932.  
   
