As much as you are or may be right on the rest of the stuff you say, 
the above is not correct. Many (*many*) UNIX programs will use $TMP 
or $TMPDIR if set. In fact, I use this behaviour all the time to make
them use a private directory that I create in /tmp when logging in 
and that I remove when logging out. This helps to avoids sensitive
data floating around after I'm gone.

