In article <3eeeh4$nk9@hdxu03.telecom.ptt.nl> spee001@telecom.ptt.nl (Jan Willem Spee,HD0.83c,050-855828) writes:

> Does anyone know if there is an (default) upper limit to the size of
> an input or output parameter in a DCE RPC Call?  If so, what is this
> limit? Is there a way to change it?  I would be very grateful if
> someone could help me on this question.

	There is no architected limit to the size of parameters in RPC.
I do not know if any implementation imposes a limit -- if one did that
would be a bug.

	Since there is a limit on datagram size using, the RPC protocol
must handle fragmentation and reassembly when using the UDP transport.
This is how RPC supports arbitrarily-sized parameters in RPC requests.
