>   Whats the minimum hardware requirement?

80-100MB disk [for a fairly complete installation, including X.  lop off
about 35MB if you don't want X] and 8MB of ram.  diskette-and-ram only
versions are possible and will likely become common as amateur radio IP
packet switches/nodes.

>   Lastly, if UNIX is soooo good, then why doesn't everybody run it.

no one is going to make you do things you feel uncomfortable with on
your computer.  do what you like -- more than likely everyone here
couldn't care less.  but if you are sick and tired of having to reset
your computer every 3 hours because the program you used has crashed,
if you are fed up with having to keep 19 copies of AUTOEXEC.BAT and
