"Ronald D. Kurr" <kurr@ctron.com> writes:

>From the literature I've read, it seems that a DCE client can make a
>non-blocking RPC call.  What I haven't been able to find out is whether
>a call-back mechanism is used or if the client programmer is expected
>to make use of DCE threads to achieve the parallelism?  Please send
>responses to kurr@ctron.com.

The usual approach is to have the client spawn a new thread and
let the thread make a blocking RPC.  All RPCs in DCE are blocking.
You could also program the server to return quickly, do the real work
asynchronously, then make a callback, if that seemed appropriate.

I've crossposted to comp.soft-sys.dce, which is the more appropriate
newsgroup for DCE questions.

