to the memory limitations of standard, 16-bit DOS.  The same 16-bit
DOS that you have two viable choices today to circumvent:  Get a free
C compiler for your 386 that was written for UNIX, or buy yourself an
expensive compiler (Watcom, the one that DOS4GW comes from, is $895)

