Linux, a POSIX-compliant UNIX operating system with a price-tag of
$0.00...

It runs on a 386 or better processor, and on systems with more than 4
megabytes of physical memory.  Some insist that the 'minimum system'
to run it well is a 486SX or DX with 8 megs.

And this is about what you need to run a lot of software today in the
DOS world.  Will Windows 95 run acceptably on a 386SX-33 with 4 megs
memory and 120 megs hard drive?  Not that we'll know till '96 or so.

For those of you from another planet (or newsgroup), if you're
interested in Linux take a look at this file:
