accomodate any number of connections at the same time.  Fax modem
softare exists but I've never used it.  I'm enough of a unix weenie to
say that mv, cp, tar, g(un)zip, ... are all I want, instead of a zip
manager or file manager.  I don't know what hytelnet is, but I can use
gopher, mosaic, lynx, ... to access www resources.  Is that what hytelnet
is?  As for viruses, none are known for Linux.  THe UNIX mindset
doesn't allow for DOS-style virii to propogate, since most of the time
the user runs programs installed by and writable only by the
superuser.  Also, when you install most of your software from source,
there's not as much of an opportunity for (binary) virii to come
along.

